    "done_when": "Reported by s22-coord: tests/test_discovery_cache.py::test_repeat_discovery_skips_git_and_metadata_for_all_mounts fails at main. Its stub `counted_parse(path)` (about line 96) replaces serve._plan_html.parse_meta with one argument. Since 8ac88e011 (resource-identity-reads-the-digest-index), reckon/metadata_index.py parse_meta_shared calls _plan_html.parse_meta(path, slug) with two. The digest-keyed memo there (_META_BY_DIGEST) is process-global, so in a whole-suite run an earlier test can have cached the same content. The stub is then never called and the test passes by order; run alone it fails. The node makes the stub accept the slug argument the shipped call passes, and forward it, and clears the shared digest memo at the start of the test, through metadata_index's own clear function, so the count no longer depends on earlier tests. Every assertion the test makes about skipped git and metadata calls on repeat discovery is kept. It changes no product file. The file passes run alone, and again when run after tests/test_resource_identity_reads_the_digest_index.py in one process, both logged. The declared negative control is executed and logged.",
    "estimated_hours": 0.5,
